A fixture config defines a macro as a real shell command (``echo 1``); the CLI subprocess
executes the command and writes the output into the frontmatter, proving live macro
execution through the subprocess boundary.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  macros:
    one: ["echo", "1"]
-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
---
# Body
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md 'value={{ macro("core.macros.one") }}'
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ---
 title: Foo
+value: 1
 ---
 # Body
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: value=1
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
value: 1
---
# Body
